# =====================================================================
# CRG workspace .gitignore
# =====================================================================

# === P0 EMERGENCY (added 2026-05-01) ===
# Untracked scratchpads containing live production secrets.
# Never commit. Rotate keys via Levite, then delete the dirs entirely.
deploy-functions-tmp/
04-PEPTIDES/

# === Scratchpad / backup patterns ===
*-tmp/
*-scratch/
*-WIP/
**/BACKUP-*/
**/src-BACKUP-*/
**/*-BACKUP-*.html
**/*-BACKUP-*.js

# === Secrets — defense in depth ===
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# === Local Netlify folder ===
.netlify

# === Node ===
node_modules/

# === macOS ===
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# === IDE / editors ===
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# === builder-control local telemetry (Layer 3/4) ===
# Machine-local evidence, not shared history. The watchdog reads these on the
# machine that produced them; committing them would let one Mac's bypass record
# masquerade as another's.
builder-control/.receipts/
builder-control/bypass.log
builder-control/watchdog.log

# === builder-control workflow backups ===
# A dated backup is required before editing an enforcement workflow, so that a
# bad edit to the gate can be reverted without relying on the gate that was just
# edited. The backup is machine-local safety, not shared history: committing it
# would put a second, stale copy of the workflow in the repo, and "which one is
# the gate?" is exactly the duplicate-authority failure single-authority-check
# exists to catch.
.github/workflows/*.bak-*

# === AEGIS dashboard generated state ===
# state.js is a timestamped snapshot produced by aegis-state.cjs. It is
# regenerable, machine-local, and changes on every run because it carries
# `generatedAt` — so tracking it would make the review subject hash change for
# reasons that have nothing to do with the code, invalidating bound reviews on
# every refresh. The slice REQUIRES it to render (that is the point: no state,
# no dashboard), and dashboard-slice.test.cjs fails if it is missing, so this
# cannot quietly become a dashboard with no data source.
builder-control/dashboard/state.js

# Attestation key — machine-local, never committed.
builder-control/.attestation-key

builder-control/ledger.json.lock
builder-control/ledger.json.tmp-*

# Transient test fixtures — must never enter a subject diff.
builder-control/.test-*.json
